==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
From Germanic ''*maga-'' ‘kin’.  Cognate with [[Middle Dutch]] ''[[maech]]'' (Dutch [[maag]]), [[Old High German]] ''[[māg]]'', Gothic [[𐌼𐌴𐌲𐍃]]<!--displaying as four question marks; does one need a special font for this?--> ‘son-in-law’.

